{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"comparable-dendritic-roach","creation_channel":"python","description":"# Inbound title is reverted by outbound local-wins, so a Jira-side summary edit never reaches the local ticket\n\n## Symptom\n\nLive against the Jira Data Center harness (run 30724309686),\n`tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_mutations.py::test_inbound_mutation_round_trips[02-edit-summary]`\nfails: a DC summary edit, confirmed present in the JQL index, does not reach the bound local\nticket's `.title` after a clean writing pass. The sibling `[03-edit-description]` PASSES on the\nsame fixture and the same pass, as do add/remove-label, comment, assign and unassign. The\nfailure is title-specific.\n\n## Proven root cause\n\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_field_diff.py:38-45` defined the arbitration set as\n`_INBOUND_MIRRORED_FIELDS = frozenset({\"description\", \"priority\", \"status\", \"assignee\"})` and its\ncomment declared `title` \"deliberately absent\", on the grounds that the pre-625b differ iterated\nJira-shaped keys (whose title key is `summary`, never a member of the local-named set) so title\nwas never suppressed, and that behaviour was preserved verbatim.\n\nThe guard `_suppressed_by_inbound` (`outbound_field_diff.py:247-256`) is membership-gated on that\nset, and the title comparison at `outbound_field_diff.py:265-268` sat OUTSIDE every guard. So when\na teammate edits the Jira summary while local is unchanged since the baseline, the outbound differ\nemits `title = <stale local value>`. The inbound differ then DROPS its own correct title update as\na contradiction of a just-emitted outbound change for the same target: `inbound_differ.py:483-486`\nmaps outbound `summary` to inbound `title`, and `inbound_differ.py:653-656` filters it out\n(bidirectional suppression, bug 3bf8).\n\nTwo consequences, only the first of which the live cell observed:\n\n1. the Jira-side title never reaches the local ticket; and\n2. the stale local title is pushed back over the Jira edit.\n\n## Why description passes and title does not\n\n`description` IS in the set, the fixture's local description equals the baseline, so\n`_suppressed_by_inbound` returns True, no outbound description is emitted, and the inbound\ndescription flows. That is the whole asymmetry.\n\n## Authority violated\n\n`docs/adr/0026-reconciler-three-way-merge-baseline.md:21-31` names the arbitrated set as \"the five\ninbound-mirrored scalar fields (title/description/priority/status/assignee)\" and mandates: local ==\nbaseline means the outbound push is SUPPRESSED so the inbound differ mirrors it; local != baseline\nmeans local-wins. `docs/jira-sync-setup.md:269` documents Title as syncing Jira to Local. Not\nDC-specific: the module is vendor-neutral, so Cloud reverts a Jira-side summary edit identically.\n\n## Runtime proof\n\nDriving `diff_canonical_fields` directly with local title == baseline title and a differing remote\ntitle returned `{'title': 'OLD'}`; the same call with description varied instead returned `{}`.\nFeeding that outbound emission into `compute_inbound_mutations` returned `[]` with\n`suppression_count == 1`, versus `[{'title': 'NEW-from-jira'}]` with no outbound context.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- With a baseline carrying `title` and local `title` matching it, a differing remote title emits NO\n  outbound `title`; the inbound differ mirrors it into the local ticket.\n- local `title` != baseline `title` still emits local-wins outbound (unchanged).\n- No baseline, or a baseline omitting `title`, still degrades to local-wins (unchanged).\n- A unit test on the LIVE canonical path (`outbound_field_diff`), not on the production-dead\n  `adapters/jira/outbound_fields._diff_fields`.\n","id":"b9b8-1c40-ea53-4ef3","parent_id":"e369-a449-4773-48fb","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"inbound title reverted by outbound local-wins"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785645362885447001,"uuid":"ed951cf3-b869-417f-850c-43357fbdb0db"}